<svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.526ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 2000.7 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"5B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(278,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1222.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1722.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"5D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5D\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.\n\n<br><br>We want to find the maximum and minimum perimeters of such triangles, which occur at <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.282ex\" height=\"1.441ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -626 2334.6 637\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(638.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1694.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.13ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2267.6 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(638.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1694.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, respectively.\n\n<br><br>To find the minimum perimeter, we use a geometric approach. Reflect point <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.717ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 759 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> over the line <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.464ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.27ex\" height=\"1.995ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 2329.6 882\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D466\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D466\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(773.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1829.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> to get <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=